{
  "id": "queue-kanji-first-deckless",
  "title": "Kanji before their first word for a deckless note and for a deck entry, whatever add_kanji says (ADR-040)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_first_deckless"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 6. Note 1 is the deckless vocab note 学校 (card ...10, new). The user deck \"Words\" has add_kanji \"off\" (deprecated, not read) and holds the entries 先生 and うっかり without notes. No kanji note exists.",
    "Step 0: the deck and the deckless source take turns (deck first). The deck draws the entry 先生 as the unit 先, 生, 先生 (3 of the 6); the deckless source draws 学校 as the unit 学, 校, 学校 (6 of 6); the entry うっかり no longer fits the goal: the kanji count against it. The fetch mints the four kanji notes (origin auto_kanji) and the note of 先生 and serves kanji immediately before their word: 先 生 先生 学 校 学校. until_stop is 6.",
    "kanji_parts of 学校 (ADR-041): 学 uses its on reading ガク as がっ, 校 uses コウ as こう. front_furigana is false (both kanji are learnable).",
    "Step 1: the same fetch again mints nothing: the same six cards (the minted ids differ between the sides and are renamed by the normalisation).",
    "Step 2: getDeck carries progress (ADR-041): two deck words (先生 has a new card, うっかり has no note), none learned."
  ],
